{"ref":"BDB, נֹ֫עַר","hw":"נֹ֫עַר","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">נֹ֫עַר</span></big>  <strong>n.m. youth, early life</strong> (rare poet. synon. for <span dir=\"rtl\">נְעוּרִים</span>);—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">נ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 33:25\" href=\"/Job.33.25\">Jb 33:25</a> (= youthful vigour), <a data-ref=\"Job 36:14\" href=\"/Job.36.14\">36:14</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מִנּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 29:21\" href=\"/Proverbs.29.21\">Pr 29:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 88:16\" href=\"/Psalms.88.16\">ψ 88:16</a> <em>from youth up</em>.","next":"BDB, נַעֲרָה","prev":"BDB, נַ֫עַר²"}